  see <strong>CMUCL</strong> and <strong>CLISP</strong> are not supported,
  and neither are several other implementations purportedly supported by <strong>Bordeaux Threads</strong>.<br />
  
  (1) Apparently, <strong>SBCL</strong>, <strong>CCL</strong> and <strong>ACL</strong> do not have full a
  <em>recursive</em> locks API; it seems all locks are such.  The missing bits
  are different and this is reflected in the number of tests actually
  performed.  In the future the regular API may be used and the missing
  tests will just work.<br />
  
  (2) The <code>timeout</code> tests for <strong>ABCL</strong> sometime fail unexpectedly; this
  is probably due to the fact that <code>sleep</code> is quite finicky both at the
  <strong>CL</strong> and the <strong>Java</strong> level.  Tracking down why is left as an
  exercise for the <strong>ABCL</strong> developers (not the only one they have been assigned: hint, hint).
