<h2>How Did I Get Here?</h2>

<p>Before AI stuff I used some testing frameworks to tortur... pardon, evaluate students' projects (yes, I inflict <strong>CL</strong>
  on them). Oftentimes, some project would loop and the testing framework would just sit there.  A check of most <strong>CL</strong>
  testing framworks showed (I may be wrong) that they lacked a proper <em>timout</em> machinery (some declare it, but deep down it
  is fake).</p>

<p>I thus set out to create a portable <code>with-timeout</code> macro. That was the mistake that led to <strong>Threadmi&lambda;</strong>.</p>

<p>Now, <strong>testing frameworks</strong> developers have no more excuses.</p>


